  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1230 PM CST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nWarming trend begins Sunday with above normal temperatures\nreturning and persisting through mid next week. The upper low\ncurrently across far SW TX will weaken as it slowly evolves\nnortheastward and the majority of guidance keep any rains well\nsouth of the local area. A fast moving wave will move across the\nregion Tuesday night or Wednesday with a low chance of light rain.\n\nStronger ridging aloft is forecast to develop across the western\nCONUS placing dry and cooler northwesterly flow aloft downstream.\nThis will act to reinforce the airmass change behind the Wednesday\nwave and bring cooler temperatures, nearer to seasonal normals, \nfor late week into next weekend. Dry weather also appears likely\nto continue into next weekend.",
